	(text "PWN output pin has an internal 4.7k pull-up resistor\n\nR69 is a current-limiting/damping resistor \n(100R is a common \"damping resistor\" value to blunt fast edge rates \nand reduce high-frequency rining/overshoot.\n\nFAN1_TAC input pin is open-drain and needs a pull-up resistor.\n\nD26 protects against voltage surges. If TAC signal exceeds 5V+0.7V,\nthe diode conducts and diverge surge current to power rail.\n\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30.226 51.816 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
